        "type": "4-Mark Interpretation Difference",
        "marks": 4,
        "targetMins": 5,
        "questionText": "Study Interpretations 1 and 2. They give different views about the methods and community impact of the Black Panther Party. What is the main difference between these views? Explain your answer, using details from both interpretations.",
        "stimulus": [],
        "sourceExtract": "<div><div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\"><strong>Interpretation 1:</strong> From a modern historical study.</div><div>The Black Panther Party achieved prominence through its emphasis on armed self-defense and community monitoring. Composed primarily of urban youth, the party directly challenged police practices by conducting armed patrols to observe arrests. This confrontational stance led to several violent encounters with law enforcement, including a fatal shootout in 1967.</div></div><hr style=\"border:none; border-top:1px dashed #cbd5e1; margin:12px 0;\"><div><div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\"><strong>Interpretation 2:</strong> From a different historical perspective.</div><div>Beyond their militant public image, the Black Panthers dedicated significant resources to community welfare. They operated free health clinics, distributed clothing, and organized food programs to support low-income neighborhoods. These grassroots initiatives addressed immediate social needs while promoting Black pride and education among community youth.</div></div>",
        "modelAnswer": "The main difference is that <strong>Interpretation 1</strong> focuses on militant confrontation, arguing the Black Panthers gained prominence through \"armed self-defense and community monitoring\" that led to violent clashes with police. In contrast, <strong>Interpretation 2</strong> focuses on constructive grassroots aid, arguing that beyond their militant image the Panthers dedicated \"significant resources to community welfare\" through free clinics, clothing drives, and food programs.",
        "pdfUrl": "/pdfs/mocks/usa/usa_mock_4_question_booklet.pdf",
        "mockUrl": "/units/usa/usa_mock_4_question_booklet.html"
